    "created_at": "2023-03-23T10:52:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-23T10:52:17Z",
    "body": "I think the relevant question is whether there are use cases for discriminating the error types coming out of the stream. If so, using separate exception types is worthwhile. If not, sticking with the generic, default `TypeError` makes sense.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
