    "created_at": "2023-03-24T07:24:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-24T07:24:46Z",
    "body": "For someone trying to use DecompressionStream for the first time, it might be useful to distinguish between `TypeError` meaning \"you gave me something that wasn't a BufferSource\" and `DataError` meaning \"the input was not a valid compressed stream\".\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, [TextDecoderStream uses `TypeError`](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-textdecoderstream:~:text=If%20result%20is%20error%2C%20then%20throw%20a%20TypeError.) for bad input, and maybe consistency is more important here.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
